==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Executioner''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Dark Lazer''' when obtained from [[The Dom Awakens!]] (may drop on the first stage but guaranteed on the second) and is at level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Prior to her [[True Form]], Dom Cat is almost useless due to her very low DPS. She can still be used effectively in [[Empire of Cats]], where she is first made available, but there's still no incentive to purchase her as other units get the job done more effectively.

==='''True Form'''===
Dark Lazer is a very powerful cat, being able to pull off incredible DPS against 2 types of enemies, something useful to have as both Red and Dark enemies become big threats in mid-late [[Stories of Legend]]. Despite this, she still struggles within her niche, as her health and single knockback prevent her from living to deliver her damage for long. Although, her singular knockback allows her to serve as a tanker thanks to her [[Strong Against|Strong VS]] ability, and her slow speed would make it harder for her to reach the frontline if she could be juggled. Additionally, being a single target unit with short range, she can't handle enemy rangers, swarms or high DPS foes like [[Capy]], [[Gory Dark]] and [[Razorback]] unless you have them stunned or weakened.

With full Treasures, Dark Lazer at level 50 deals 16,042.5 DPS against [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] and [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemies.

Aside from being used to tackle enemies in her target traits, Dark Lazer is also included in the [[Power of Darkness (Combo)|Power of Darkness]] [[Cat Combo]], a good asset for Weaken-based strategies, which make use of [[:Category:Cats with Weaken ability|Cats with the Weaken ability]], such as [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Cat Jobs]], [[Driller Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Power Driller Cat]] and [[Otaku Geek Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hacker Geek Cat]].

==='''Talents'''===
With full Attack Buff, a level 50 Dark Lazer deals '''28,876.5 DPS''' against Red and Dark enemies, a very good use of your NP. However, you need to make full use of your NP and go all the way investing in her, otherwise her damage and survivability will falter through late Stories of Legend and [[Uncanny Legends]] to the point where she will be demolished in seconds. They are also very expensive, so they may not be worth the price until the time is right, such as in {{4c}} stages where your selection of attackers is limited.

Her impressive attack speed works perfectly with her [[Wave Attack]] Talent, where a stack of Dark Lazers against any [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] or [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Barrier]]-wielding enemies can rack up destructive DPS thanks to her quick attack rate and somewhat low damage per hit. She can also be stacked on the [[UltraBaaBaa]] to launch an immense amount of Wave Attacks against backliners or superbackliners. However, be wary when using her against backliners like Director Kurosawah, as her damage will be too little to stagger them unless stacked, although the presence of frontliners still allow her to generate waves. The only Talent that may be unnecessary is Weaken Immunity, as it is rare for her to need it due to the scarcity of Red/Dark enemies that have this ability, although it could possibly be used against [[Hannya]] in [[Realm of Carnage (Deadly)|Realm of Carnage]] and [[Wrath of Carnage (Deadly)|Wrath of Carnage]] stages to quickly destroy the boss along with any red support. This can also be quite useful against [[Dark Dober]], however there are too few options to make this talent worth it.

Cost Down is certainly useful, as Dark Lazer is a huge resource drain. It's best to leave it at level 8, where her cost reaches 1200¢, as she remains usable in specific [[Cats of the Cosmos]] [[Restriction Stage]]s balanced around said price point.

==='''Orb'''===
Strong Against Black or Red effect Orb is the best option in most situations. Cost Down or Cash Back is a good Orb to alleviate cash drain.

