==Trivia==
*[[Bondage Cat (Special Cat)|Bondage Cat]], Dom Cat, [[Ninja Cat (Special Cat)|Ninja Cat]] and [[Zombie Cat (Special Cat)|Zombie Cat]] all had their Strong Against ability removed in [[Version 2.0 Update|Version 2.0]] and readded in [[Version 2.0 Update#Version 2.0.7 Update|Version 2.0.7]].
*Before [[Version 3.6 Update|Version 3.6]] of [[Nyanko Daisensou]], Dark Lazer had [[Area Attack]].
*Dark Lazer's description misspells the word "fluorescent" as "fl'''ou'''rescent".
*Dom Cat and Executioner were given Multi-Hit in [[Version 6.0 Update|Version 6.0]].
**Despite seemingly striking 4 times per attack, both only hit 3 times. This is because 3 is the most amount of Multi-Hit strikes that a unit can have in the files.
*Executioner Cat's mask is a reference to [[wikipedia:Jason Voorhees|Jason Voorhees]].
*Dark Lazer is a reference to [[wikia:starwars:Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] from [[wikipedia:Star Wars|Star Wars]].
**Interestingly, the usable Dark Lazer wields a blue lightsaber, while its enemy counterpart featured in various event stages accurately portrays Darth Vader with a red one. This is likely due to blue lightsabers being seen as a force for good, with red as a force for evil.
*Dom Cat has received numerous name changes over many games, often due to the overtly sexual nature of her theming:
**In [[Battle Cats (Removed Game)|Battle Cats]], Dom Cat was named SM Cat, short for Sadomasochism. She was renamed to Dom Cat in [[The Battle Cats]] possibly due to domination representing only the S part of SM (the M, of course, being [[Bondage Cat (Special Cat)|Bondage Cat]]).
**In the spinoff [[Go! Go! Pogo Cat]], she is renamed to Mistress Cat, seemingly to get the rating down to "E" for everyone.
**In [[The Battle Cats Unite!]], she is renamed to Queen Cat, also to make it more kid-friendly. Funnily enough, this is an exact match with her Japanese name.
*The swing effect on Executioner's axe has a black dot mistakenly placed off to the right. This is visible in-game as a black dot appearing next to their arm during their attack animation.
*In the Nintendo Switch port, Dark Lazer is still usable as a True Form albeit only through save file editing.

